    "decoder_context": [
      "Real inner-product spaces carry the stated norm, real scalar multiplication and canonical Borel sigma algebra when those typeclasses are present. NNReal denotes nonnegative reals; coercions to real are written with an up-arrow. ContDiff R 2 means genuine twice continuously Frechet differentiability; gradient and iterated fderiv are the genuine first and second derivatives under that hypothesis. LipschitzWith1 means nonexpansive.",
      "Fin J is the finite index0,...,J-1. Lagrange.basis(univ,t,j) is the real polynomial product over k!=j of C((t_j-t_k)^(-1))*(X-C(t_k)); ell.eval s is real polynomial evaluation. sSup is the real supremum of the indicated image on the closed interval. The displayed interval integrals use real Lebesgue measure, with oriented endpoints."
